.TH HEAD 1 "September 2026" "mitos-utils 0.1.0" "MITOS User Commands"
.SH NAME
head \- output the first part of files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B head
[\fB\-n\fR \fIN\fR|\fB\-c\fR \fIN\fR] [\fIFILE\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Print the first 10 lines of each FILE to standard output; with more than one FILE, precede each with a header giving its name.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-n \fIN\fR
Print the first N lines instead of 10.
.TP
.B \-c \fIN\fR
Print the first N bytes instead (binary-safe).
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
Every mitos-utils command additionally accepts \fB\-\-help\fR (print a usage line and exit) and \fB\-\-version\fR. Commands that take file/path arguments also accept \fB\-\-\fR to mark the end of options, so a file literally named e.g. \fB\-oddfile\fR can still be referenced.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on a general failure (a listed file could not be processed, etc.), 2 on a usage error (missing or invalid arguments).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mitos\-box (1),
.BR mitos\-utils\-compat (7),
.BR mitos\-utils\-integration (7)
